173: def want_rldimi(rs_val, ra_val, sh, mb):
174:     """Book I :4319 -- m <- MASK(b, not n), i.e. MASK(MB, 63-SH): INCLUSIVE and WRAPPING.
175: 
176:        *** CORRECTED 2026-09-11.  This computed `mask_b_63(mb) & mask_0_e(63-sh)' -- the
177:        INTERSECTION -- which is EMPTY for every wrapping encoding: 2016 of 4096 (MB, SH)
178:        pairs, 49.2% of the space, produced the all-zero mask Book I :4031 forbids.  The
179:        oracle then returned the untouched destination and would have AGREED with any
180:        implementation that also omitted the wrap. ***
181: 
182:        The prose at :4323-4324 ("1 bits from bit MB through bit 63-SH") describes the
183:        NON-WRAPPING reading, and quoting it beside the formula is how the error got in;
184:        :4022-4029 is the definition that governs.  The PEM citation the old docstring
185:        carried (:29908) is superseded: PEM :302 names Book I as the defining manual."""
