209:        BEING CORRECTED, cut off before it says what was wrong.  Recover it from
210:        `git show' on the 2026-09-11 revision if the clause is ever needed. ***]
211:        *** CORRECTED 2026-09-17 by the grok seat, which went and READ the artifact. ***
212:        An earlier wording here said this was "Measured against the SHIPPED X(rlwinm)" on
213:        "131072 of 131072 cells".  **THE WORD `Measured' IS NOT SUPPORTED BY THE ARTIFACT.**
214:        `artifacts/ppcwitnessmaskoracle/ENUMERATION_20260911.txt' contains ZERO occurrences of
215:        131072, and says of itself at :49: "it is a MODEL enumeration, not an emulator
216:        measurement.  No binary was built".  The identity is ALGEBRA -- the old `mask32' simply
217:        IS the shipped handler's mask-and-zero-extend, so the two agree by construction, for
218:        every source and not merely for 2^17 encodings.
219:        *** THE REPAIR IS STILL WARRANTED, AND BY A STRONGER ARGUMENT THAN THE NUMBER WAS. ***
220:        It is warranted by that IDENTITY WITH THE SHIPPED HANDLER -- an oracle that is a copy of
221:        the implementation it grades cannot go red against it, which is this project's
222:        check-that-cannot-fail shape in its purest form.  A count of agreeing cells was never the
223:        reason and, stated as a measurement, was a WRONG RECORD of the score-claim class: a number
224:        in a measured column that no run produced.
225: 
226:        Book I gives rlwinm at :4126-4128 and rlwimi at :4316-4318 with the IDENTICAL mask
227:        term, and ROTL32 (:501-504) produces the low word DUPLICATED into both halves.
228:        MB, ME are 5-bit, so mstart/mstop lie in 32..63; when MB > ME the mask covers
229:        MB+32..63 AND 0..ME+32, and that second range contains every position 0..31 -- the
230:        whole high half -- so the rotated word lands there.
231: 
232:        *** :4033-4035 IS NOT A COUNTER-TEXT, THOUGH IT READS LIKE ONE. ***  It says the
233:        mask "start and stop POSITIONS are always in the low-order 32 bits" -- true, they
234:        are 32..63 -- and says nothing about where the 1-bits reach.  :4015 says the mask
235:        is 64 bits long and :4026-4028 gives the wrap explicitly.
236: 
237:        BOOK I'S CLEARING SENTENCES ARE SCOPED; THE PEM'S IS UNCONDITIONAL.  Book I has
238:        TWO, at :4195-4196 (rlwinm) and :4291-4292 (rlwnm), each inside a Programming Note
239:        and each qualified "for all the uses given above" -- and every enumerated use fixes
240:        a NON-WRAPPING (MB, ME).  The 2005 PEM carries the qualified form at :30074 AND an
241:        unconditional one at :30065; it is the unconditional claim that Book I lacks.
242:        **Book I states no clearing for rlwimi at all** -- its entry (:4304-4358) is RTL only.
243: 
244:        ONE SHARED HELPER FEEDS BOTH want_rlwinm AND want_rlwimi, DELIBERATELY: the manual
