83: ### 7n-2.3  The rule, and why the author's split is wrong in both halves
84: 
85: > **A claimed-but-unmeasured floor clause is L4 exactly when the record asserts a MEASUREMENT or a NUMBER that was not made.  A claim that a clause is carried BY CONSTRUCTION is a claim about the instrument's shape, checked by READING -- the gate's pin form (equality, not `check_min`) plus a row that reds on a dead run, or an `#include` of the product plus a gate that reds on compile failure -- and it is L2 only when that reading fails or a run comes back green.  Bare clause letters beside row names are neither: a new round writes "(c): measured at <artifact>" or "(c): by construction via <row/pin>, leg not run", never "(c) -- `live`".**
