89: **So the measuring seat's FLOOR grade of the tile-index family was wrong AS A GRADE, and the codex class-closure review of 2026-09-11 was right** (*"BECAUSE THE BODY NEVER TESTS `tile_nr` FOR ZERO, `M30` ... IS NOT A FLOOR AXIS UNDER THE BODY-TESTED-PARTITION RULE -- IT IS CLAUSE-(e) DEBT"*).  The data-flow sentence the seat used (*"flows into the address operand at least as directly as `tlb_mode` does"*) is the 2026-09-09 LABEL clause with its first half dropped: a dispatch LABEL becomes a floor axis when its value flows into a body-read lvalue -- `tlb_mode` is a label the body tests as a case AND flows into `tileptr`; `tile_nr` flows and is not tested as a case.  Flow alone is the transitive-chasing reading the 08-24 bound forbids.
90: 
91: **Harder on the author's leaning, as the brief asks.**  The author leaned YES (floor, L2, a repair owing its own pass).  YES would have reopened a chain the receipt closed ("NO FURTHER PASS IS OWED") on a mutant that no instrument in the tree can see; it would grade by consequence, which D1 refused; and its warrant is the rejected finiteness bound.  And harder on NO, because NO carries a real cost: `ok || (tileptr & 0xfff00000)` keeps the instrument green while re-opening the uninitialised-`buf` store on every real framebuffer tile at a physical address `>= 1 MB` -- the `M30` shape (fix kept on the instrument, open on the world).  The carrier's answer to that is the one it gave at `#549`: severity ORDERS the debt and does not promote it.  So the row is filed at the TOP of this file's coverage debt, below its live defects (`sgirebufuninit`, med), and it costs ONE readback.
92: 
93: **What was legitimately done anyway.**  The 59 -> 77 -> 89 repairs were L1 (pre-ship construction: fd15065 landed 09-12, after all of them), licensed by the round's own choice on a severity finding (98.75% of the screen re-opened by `M30`).  L1 permits strengthening for any reason; only the floor MANDATES.  Nothing the round did was wrong; what it recorded about WHY was.
94: 
95: **EXHAUSTED / SAMPLED: ADOPTED as clause-(e) disclosure vocabulary, with one correction.**  It is exactly what clause (e) asks for -- *"write into the CONTRACT which cells are covered and which are deliberately not"* -- made explicit per axis.  Definitions: EXHAUSTED := every cell of the BODY-TESTED partition of that lvalue is rowed (floor discharged on that axis); SAMPLED := driven at two or more values, with the untested slices and their derived or measured sweeps named.  The probe's `:587` wording "every value in the reachable domain is driven" coincides with the partition definition for `tlb_mode`/`bufdepth`/`color_mode` (tiny domains) and must not be the definition: the next probe with a 2^32 operand could never write EXHAUSTED under it and would write it anyway for a 16-value field the body tests at one bound.  BOUND: a disclosure vocabulary can never DEMAND a row (the carrier's filter rule: *"a filter can reject or repair a row; it can never demand a new one"*), so it cannot grow.  STRUCTURAL LANDING SPOT, per the structure-first rule: the PRETABLE block's GUARD FIELD vs BODY FIELD check gains one column, "partition the BODY induces on this lvalue" (the codex 09-11 table is the exemplar), and EXHAUSTED/SAMPLED is read off that column rather than asserted.  A template line, not a checker.
96: 
97: ### 4. Measurable consequences, in order.
98: 
99: 1. **Records, L4, three sites, in the closure-records commit the row already owes:** (i) `sgirandomcolour` note line "genuine floor-shaped gap ... Filed as OWED" -> "(e) under D1 2026-09-25: bit 31 is the only tested bit of `tileptr` and is constant-cleared at `:319`; equivalent to the fix on every driven row by inspection; one-row debt, filed"; and the "GRADED FLOOR" / "finite" sentences for `M30`-`M33` -> L1 strengthening on a severity warrant; (ii) probe `:610-617` -> one note that the `:26-28` contract supersedes it and the species is (e) (the `#556` hrecord vehicle); (iii) `pass2_ledger.tsv:159` disclosure list -> add the SAMPLED axes and the four derived sweeps.
100: 2. **File ONE debt row** (`sgirecontentslice` or similar), ranked at the top of this file's coverage debt and below `sgirebufuninit`: four readbacks in existing sessions -- a descriptor `>= 0x8010` (physical `>= 0x100000`) at an already-rowed cell (kills the array-contents slice and adds a second anchored address), an odd-`x` cell, a `y` with bit 1 set, a mode word with bit 0 set -- one re-table, scores MEASURED, pin 89 -> 93.  Not in-round, not L2, no pass reopened; it ships the next time a measuring seat opens this instrument.
101: 3. **Released:** the repair pass the queue entry said the TLB-contents gap "owes"; any class-closure demand over `(x, y)`.
102: 4. **Carrier, one sentence under the joint-cells clause, with the structural column above:** *"A derived input (a local computed from the function's inputs and feeding a body-read operand) is graded by the partition the body induces on IT, never by the flow that reaches it: `#519`'s `tile_nr`, tested only at `< 256`, is clause (e); the finite-row-set warrant is the 09-04 finiteness bound and buys nothing in either direction."*
103: 
