23: #  POST-FIX BEHAVIOUR: an unhandled / unimplemented colour mode during a PUT declines and skips
24: #  writing to memory, leaving the destination pre-paint intact.
25: #
26: #  CONTRACT -- #519 closure design, 2026-09-12.  This is the controlling coverage
27: #  contract; older CONTRACT/CLOSED/COMPLETE claims below are historical and are
28: #  superseded wherever they claim a larger domain or describe missing coverage.
29: #
30: #  The declined-PUT input projection is
31: #      {TLB_A, TLB_B, TLB_C, LIN_A} x {bufdepth 1, 2, 4, 8 bytes}
32: #      x {SGIRE_W_BADCOLOR clear, set ON ENTRY to the colour default arm}.
33: #  Its 32 cells concern PUTs that reach that arm with eligible coordinates and
34: #  a valid selected mapping.  Earlier bounds, mapping and BADMODE returns are
35: #  outside this projection.  The added fixtures use solid 1x1 DE rectangles at
36: #  (0,0); their supported RGBA/4-byte controls verify the selected destination.
37: #  At (0,0), the index and offset are zero at every tested depth.
38: #
39: #  The design occupies every cell of this projection.  This exhausts its input
40: #  tuples for a default-store permission predicate depending ONLY on these
41: #  three axes.  It is not full closure over arbitrary predicates on all function
42: #  inputs, nor a claim that each cell independently tests every warning property.
43: #  The projection's cell readbacks cover every attempted transfer byte,
44: #  including both words at depth eight.  Each added decline is observed before
45: #  a later repaint or PUT.
46: #  Preserved bytes do not prove that no write occurred: a write of identical
47: #  bytes remains invisible.  Zero-initialized negative controls have exact,
48: #  differing readbacks; kills of uninitialized-buffer mutants need measurement.
49: #
50: #  OUTSIDE: exhaustive coordinates, tile indices, descriptor payloads, raw mode
